// Concrete-Receiver Devirtualization of `dyn Trait` Vtable Calls, Indirect Function Pointers,
// and Closure Dispatch (T614 / E15.4).
// Implements SPEC-73 §§6, 8, 9 (AXS-INL-032, AXS-INL-034, AXS-INL-035;
// REQ-OPT-103..107, REQ-OPT-112..113, REQ-OPT-315):
//   - Tier 1 (`DEVIRT_TIER_EXACT`): `Certainty.Proven` single concrete target devirtualization
//     (local SSA/constructor provenance, interprocedural parameter provenance, or closed-world
//     single-implementor proof) -> direct `MIR_CONST_FN` call + immediate inliner & SROA cascade (`AXS-INL-032.1`)
//   - Tier 2 (`DEVIRT_TIER_GUARDED`): bounded multi-target speculative devirtualization (2..4 targets)
//     emitting `MIR_TERM_SWITCH_INT` guarded direct calls with exhaustive closed-world branch or
//     mandatory open-world dynamic fallback (`AXS-INL-032.2`, `REQ-OPT-106`)
//   - Tier 3 (`DEVIRT_TIER_RETAINED_DYNAMIC`): fail-closed retention of dynamic dispatch when
//     target set is unknown, open-world, `@export` boundary, or `dynamic_loading_active` (`AXS-INL-032.3`, `REQ-OPT-107`, `REQ-OPT-113`)
//   - `PassManager` `TransformationContract` (`PASS_DEVIRT = 16u16`) (`AXS-INL-034`)
//   - Deterministic `--emit=devirt` inspection printer (`devirt_print`) (`AXS-INL-035`)
module compiler.opt.devirt

